Trevor, 21 – Food Poisoning

“I got food poisoning after eating takeout one night, and it hit me way faster than I expected. Within a few hours I started feeling really nauseous and uncomfortable, and it just got worse from there. I couldn’t keep any food down and even drinking water was hard at first. I remember feeling really weak and just stuck in bed, not really able to do anything.

The worst part was how sudden it was. I went from feeling completely fine to feeling terrible in such a short time. I didn’t really know what to do at first, so I just tried to rest and wait it out. Eventually I realized I had to stay hydrated, even if it meant taking really small sips over time.

After it passed, I was still tired for a couple days, which I didn’t expect. That’s when I realized your body needs time to recover even after the main symptoms are gone.

Advice:

Be careful about where your food comes from
If you feel sick, focus on hydration first
Take small sips instead of trying to drink a lot at once
Give yourself time to recover even after you feel better

Now I’m way more careful about food safety and I don’t ignore how I feel after eating something that seems off.”
